The scripts and utilities found in the MassOS repositories are licensed under
the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later). The
individual programs which make up the MassOS system are licensed under various
different licenses. The license for each individual piece of software can be
found under the directory '/usr/share/licenses/' on a MassOS system. The
developers/maintainers of MassOS make no additional claims of copyright or
authorship over these projects, except where explicitly stated.

Most of the software in the core MassOS system is free software - either in the
public domain, or protected by a GPL-compatible license. Some exceptions are
made where the developers/maintainers feel necessary, such as to ensure support
for commonly used hardware devices. Full details of exceptions, can be found at
<https://github.com/MassOS-Linux/MassOS/wiki/MassOS-and-Free-Software>.

Every effort is made to comply with the terms of the GPL where possible. This
includes, but is not limited to, ensuring GPL-protected object code is never
directly linked, either statically or dynamically, with GPL-incompatible object
code. However, the existence of GPL and GPL-incompatible software on the same
system, when functioning as standalone projects that do not directly interact
with each other, is acceptable and is not restricted by the terms of the GPL,
despite a common misconception.

The MassOS wallpaper assets, under the directory 'backgrounds', are licensed
under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(CC-BY-SA-4.0). All backgrounds EXCEPT Futuristic and Avantgarde (plus their
variants) are (C) 2021-2022 Muhammad Hassan Murtaza <IKGissmart>. Futuristic is
(C) 2022 Daniel Massey, and Avantgarde is (C) 2025 Daniel Massey.

A copy of both licenses can be found in the files 'GPL-3.0' and 'CC-BY-SA-4.0'
respectively. These are also installed under the directory '/usr/share/massos/'
on a MassOS system.
